natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Natural Armor Rating", description: "A.R. 9+1D4. An attacker must roll above the A.R. to inflict hit point/S.D.C. damage; mega-damage weapons automatically blast through an S.D.C. based A.R." }
  - { name: "Size and Build", description: "About 5 feet (1.5 m) tall and 200 to 300 pounds (90 to 135 kg). An animal''s appearance with only a vaguely human, bipedal shape: a cat''s head, a fur covered body and a tail. 85% have human legs, arms and builds, 15% have animal-like legs; most are powerful and muscular but comparatively slender. Hands are usually (90%) fully articulated with an opposable thumb, though most (90%) have thick fingers and retractable claws. Stands and walks erect, though some (25%) run on all fours. Reduce Spd by 10% when climbing. Human speech is partial and guttural, with hissing, growling and roaring when excited, angry or scared. Lynx/Bobcat are 20% smaller; Snow Leopards 20% larger, African Lions 40% larger (typically 7 ft/2.1 m) and Tigers 60% larger (typically 8 ft/2.4 m) in height and weight. Matures at the same basic rate as a Dog Boy; life span an estimated 40 to 55 years." }
  - { name: "Bite and Claws", description: "By species, or by weapon. Lynx/Bobcat: bite 2D6 S.D.C., claw 2D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. bonus. Puma/Cougar/Mountain Lion: bite 3D6 S.D.C./hit point damage, claw 3D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. bonus. Leopard/Panther and Snow Leopard: bite 3D6 S.D.C./hit point damage, claw 2D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. bonus. African Lion: bite 3D6 S.D.C./hit point damage, claw 4D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. bonus. Tiger: the book prints no S.D.C. bite or claw figure. The P.S. and P.E. of mutant African Lions and Tigers can be genetically improved to be supernatural; then the bite does 1D6 M.D. and the claws 3D6 M.D. for lions, 4D6 M.D. for tigers." }
  - { name: "Leap", description: "From a standing position, by species. Lynx/Bobcat: 20 feet (6 m) across or 15 feet up (the book prints the metric as 6 m). Puma/Cougar/Mountain Lion: 40 feet (12 m) across or 20 feet (6 m) up. Leopard/Panther: 30 feet (9 m) across or 20 feet (6 m) up; increase the distance by 20% with a running start. Snow Leopard: 50 feet (15.2 m) across and 20 feet (6 m) high. African Lion: 20 feet (6 m) across or 15 feet (4.6 m) up. Tiger: 30 feet (9 m) across or 15 feet (4.6 m) up." }
  - { name: "Roar", description: "An African Lion''s roar can be heard up to one mile (1.6 km) away; a Tiger''s up to 1.5 miles (2 km) away." }
  - { name: "Sense Psychic and Magic Energy", description: "The Dog Boy''s ability, less developed: a constant, automatic sense for fellow psychics (I.S.P.) and for magic energy (P.P.E. spent as a spell, held in magic devices, or in people in large amounts of 80 points or more), followed like a scent to its source while the energy keeps being spent. Base Skill: 30% +5% per level of experience (roll once every melee round); halved when multiple sources are scattered throughout the sensing range. Range: 40 feet (12 m) +5 feet (1.5 m) per additional level for a psychic or magic practitioner NOT using his powers; 300 feet (91 m) +20 feet (6 m) per level for psionic and magic powers being used. Roll every 400 feet (122 m) to stay on the trail; a failed roll means the scent is lost. I.S.P.: none, automatic. Cannot Recognize Psychic Scent." }
  - { name: "Sense Supernatural Beings", description: "The Dog Boy''s ability, less acute: works like Sense Psychic and Magic Energy, tuned to the distinctive psychic scent of the supernatural. Base Skill: 54% +2% per level to identify the specific type/race of paranormal creature (alien intelligences, gods, demigods, demons, vampires and dragons included) and to detect whether a person is possessed. Tracking by this scent: 10% +2% per level, or 23% +3% per level if the being is also using psionics or magic. Range: 100 feet (30.5 m) per level when the being is using no special, magical or psionic powers; 1000 feet (305 m) +100 feet (30.5 m) per additional level when it is actively using them. Automatic and constant, no I.S.P. Close proximity to ley lines and nexus points disrupts the psychic senses." }
  - { name: "Psionics and I.S.P.", description: "Effectively a major psionic: saves vs psionic attack on a 12 or higher, with +2 to save vs psionic attack and all forms of mind control. Two powers of choice from the Sensitive category. I.S.P.: M.E. doubled, plus 2D6 per additional level. Recovers two I.S.P. per hour of activity or eight per hour of meditation or sleep." }
  - { name: "Excellent Vision and Passive Night Sight", description: "20/20 color vision with a 220 degree field of vision. The eyes amplify ambient light, seeing in darkness 6-7 times better than a human, but need some light (moon, stars, the glow of night clouds). In total darkness the cat is as blind as a human, though smell, hearing and whiskers let it get about 2-3 times better than a human could; penalties for blindness are -4 to strike, parry and dodge." }
  - { name: "Excellent Hearing", description: "Hears up to 25,000 vibrations per second (humans 20,000, dogs 35,000) and sounds up to two octaves above the highest note a human hears; the ears prick and swivel to focus on a sound, telling apart two sounds five degrees apart with 75% accuracy. Judge distance and precise location of the source: 80% +2% per level. Recognize and identify prey (animal or machine) by sound: 72% +2% per level, -20% for artificial sounds (bots, ''Borgs, jet packs, hovercycles). Both lose 10% for every 50 yards/meters (roughly 150 ft/45.7 m) between the cat and the source." }
  - { name: "Sense of Smell", description: "Fair to good: most cats smell about twice as well as a human, nothing like a canine. A tiger''s sense of smell is on par with a human''s." }
  - { name: "Sprinter", description: "Can run at double normal speed for 1D4 minutes before dropping back to normal speed." }
  - { name: "Sensitivity to Ley Line Energy", description: "Ley lines and nexus points obliterate the psychic and supernatural sensing abilities and give the cat a headache, so they cannot be used on a ley line or near a nexus; the physical senses, sight especially, are unaffected and the other psychic abilities are enhanced as usual. Most cats are nervous and on edge around places of magic. Unlike canines, cats are not vulnerable to ley line storms." }
  - { name: "Siberian Tiger", description: "Siberian tigers are resistant to cold (cold does half damage)." }
