extraction_notes: "WB13 Lone Star printed 76-79 (cache p077-p080, cache page = printed folio + 1). The Mutant Felines introduction and Special Cat Powers start on 76, the species bonuses are on 77, the Battle Cats R.C.C. block is on 78 and it runs on to the left column of 79 (the end of the equipment list, money, cybernetics, rank), ending where Kill Cats begins. Every number was read off renders of cache p077-p080. || XP: the column headed Monkey Boy Soldier / Battle Cat CS Soldier on the unnumbered Experience Tables page after printed 174 (cache p176), read off the render, lower bound of each band. || HEADING: Battle Cats R.C.C., under Mutant Felines; a race. || ATTRIBUTES as printed (Average Attribute Range, Standard Battle Cat): I.Q. 3D6, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 4D6, P.S. 4D6, P.P. 4D6, P.E. 4D6, P.B. 4D6, Spd 4D6+6 running (reduce by 10% when climbing, text). || POOLS: Hit points P.E. x2 plus 2D6 per level. S.D.C. is printed as ''P.E. attribute number plus 1D4x10 plus those gained from physical skills; some species get S.D.C. bonuses''. Stored as sdc_base ''P.E. + 1d4x10'' and NOT as bonuses.pools.sdc (judgement, the same reading the ursa-warrior draft made of the same sentence): the printed base contains the P.E. attribute, which a pool bonus of a number or one dice expression does not carry, and bonuses.pools.sdc is where each species variant states its printed extra S.D.C. Because sdc_base is stated there is no men_of_arms line. P.P.E. 3D6. A.R. 9+1D4 is natural ability text. || SPECIES (Physical Abilities and Bonuses, printed 77): six variants, Lynx/Bobcat, Puma/Cougar/Mountain Lion, Leopard/Panther, Snow Leopard, African Lion and Tiger; the class with no variant is the printed Standard Battle Cat with no species bonus. A variant''s bonuses block restates the +2 save vs psionic attack and mind control that every cat has. Attribute bonuses are stored as bonuses.attributes (dice strings). Lynx/Bobcat: +3 initiative, +1 strike and parry, +3 dodge, +2 disease, +4 horror factor, P.P. +1D4, Spd +1D6, Climbing +20% (80), Acrobatics +10% (40). Puma: +2 initiative, +2 strike and parry, +2 disease, +5 horror factor, +4D6 hit points, +5D6 S.D.C., I.Q. +1D4, P.S. +1D6, +10% Prowl (35), Climbing (70) and Swimming (60). Leopard/Panther: +4 initiative, +3 strike, +1 parry, +3 dodge, +1 attack, +3 roll with impact, +1 disease, +3 horror factor, +3D6 hit points, +4D6 S.D.C., I.Q. +1D4, P.S. +3D6, P.P. +1D4, Prowl +15% (40), Acrobatics +10% (40), climb printed as ''+30'' with no percent sign and read as +30% (90). Snow Leopard: the leopard plus another +1D6 H.P., +2D6 S.D.C. and +1D6 P.S., summed into single dice (hit points 4D6, S.D.C. 6D6, P.S. 4D6). African Lion: +2 initiative, +2 strike, +3 parry, +1 attack, +4 disease, +6 horror factor, +6D6 hit points, +1D6x10 S.D.C., P.S. +3D6, P.E. +1D6, Spd +2D6, Swimming +10% (60), Prowl +10% (35), Climbing +5% (65), tracking skills +10% (applied to both Track Animals, 40, and Track Humanoids, 45). Tiger: +4 initiative, +3 strike, +2 parry, +1 attack, +4 disease, +6 horror factor, +1D4x10 hit points, +2D4x10 S.D.C., I.Q. +1D4, P.S. +4D6, P.E. +2D6, Spd +1D6, Swimming 86%, Climbing +5% (65), Prowl +15% (40), tracking skills +15% (45 and 50). The horror factor figures are SAVES vs horror factor; the book prints no horror factor the cat projects. Size changes, leaps, roars, bite and claw damage, the supernatural P.S./P.E. option for lions and tigers and the Siberian tiger''s cold resistance are natural ability text. The Tiger paragraph prints no S.D.C. bite or claw damage; none stored. The Lynx leap prints 15 feet as 6 m; stored as printed. || PSIONICS: ''effectively major psionics'', saves on 12 or higher, +2 vs psionic attack and all forms of mind control (saves.psionics and saves.mind_control). Two powers from the Sensitive category and no later picks printed. I.S.P. is M.E. doubled, plus 2D6 per each ADDITIONAL level; regained at two per hour of activity or eight per hour of meditation or sleep. The two sensing abilities are natural ability text; the book says ''same as the Dog Boys but not as developed'' and prints its own numbers, and the description of what the sense does is restated from the Dog Boy entry on printed 33. || SKILLS: Speaks American at 90% is Language: Native Tongue 90, per_level 0. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Acrobatics 30, Running, Prowl 25, no bonus printed. Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals 20+10 = 30. Track Humanoids is Tracking (people) 25+10 = 35. Land Navigation 36+20 = 56. Wilderness Survival 30+15 = 45. W.P. Knife (Vibro-Blade), W.P. Energy Rifle, one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert or Assassin (depending on what the CS wants) is a choice of one; no upgrade price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. The skill list prints Climbing with no bonus; Natural climbers 60%/40% (ability 9) is stored as Climbing 60 with the catalog''s 5% per level, the second figure, 40%, in the skill note. Natural swimmers 50% (ability 10) is stored as Swimming 50 although Swimming is not in the printed skill list (judgement, as the ursa-warrior draft). || RELATED: four at level one, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Espionage +10, Medical (First Aid only) +5, Military +5, Pilot (Hovercraft, Truck, sail and motorboat only) +5, Rogue (any except Computer Hacking) +5, Technical (any except Computer Operation and Computer Programming) +10, Wilderness +10; Communications, Domestic, Physical, Pilot Related and W.P. any; Electrical and Science none. Motorboat is Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil and sail is Boat: Sail Type. ''Never taught to read'' applies to cats in CS service and is a restriction line, not an exclusion. SECONDARY: six at level one plus TWO at each of levels 2, 4, 8 and 11, same lists without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: ''basically the same as Dog Boys'', then the entry prints its own basic list, which is what is stored: DPM riot armor (dog-pack-dpm-riot-armor), tinted goggles or non-environmental helmet, radio as walkie-talkie, flashlight, pocket mirror, 100 ft of lightweight rope as five 20 ft lengths, four spikes and a hammer, portable language translator, survival knife, a pair of Vibro-Knives or Vibro-Claws as a choice at qty 2, knapsack, backpack, utility belt, air filter, gas mask, canteen. The printed comb is not stored: it has no catalog row and is a trivial personal item. The Vibro-Saber or Neuro-Mace many also have and the equipment available upon assignment are not stored. No firearm is in the printed list; none stored. || MONEY: the entry prints only a token monthly salary of 90-130 credits with all basic needs provided by the CS military. It does not print the Dog Boy''s ''player characters start off with two months pay'', and says cats do not have the Dog Boys'' privileges, so no starting_money is stored (the ursa-warrior reading). || Identification coding (the Dog Boys'' dual I.D. system), AWOL policy, typical missions and the deployment numbers (about 3,200 in service) are lore."
---

## Lore

The Battle Cat is Lone Star''s feline counterpart to the Dog Boy: a bipedal,
fur-covered mutant bred from lynx, puma, leopard, lion or tiger stock and
raised as a Coalition soldier. It keeps a weaker version of the canine psychic
nose for magic and the supernatural, and adds a cat''s night eyes, swivelling
ears, climbing and leaping.

What it does not share is the dog''s temperament. Cats are guarded, blunt and
fiercely independent; they stay with a group because they chose to, warm to
individuals of any species who earn it, and repay being taken for granted by
walking away or worse. Put on guard duty or behind a desk they sulk and do
half a job. Sent out alone or in a handful to scout, stalk, sabotage or hunt,
they are at their best, and that is how the Coalition uses most of them.

The army treats them as an experiment under observation rather than as
trusted troops. About 3,200 serve, half of them in Lone Star, and a cat that
goes feral is hunted down.

## GM Notes

Pick a species at creation: the six species differ widely in combat bonuses,
hit points, S.D.C. and attribute bonuses, and the standard block alone is the
bare average. Lions and tigers may, at the G.M.''s option, have supernatural
P.S. and P.E., which turns bite and claws into mega-damage attacks; the cat
itself stays an S.D.C. creature with a natural Armor Rating that mega-damage
weapons ignore.

The Dog Boy optional tables are closed to cats; only the Mutation Gone Wrong
table may be used, and only with the G.M.''s approval. The book gives no
starting money, only a token salary of 90-130 credits a month. A cat outside
Coalition service is a feral or a free-born and is killed on sight by the CS.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'battle-cat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'battle-cat';

